other studies that look at things&nbsp;
like learning, memory, plasticity —&nbsp;

02:42:19.607 --> 02:42:22.260
Tim Ferriss: For sure.
Dr. Matt Walker: — in the brain, because&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:23.160 --> 02:42:28.380
things like classic sleeping pills, like Ambien,&nbsp;
have been found to produce non-naturalistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:28.380 --> 02:42:32.760
sleep. There was obvious studies have them been&nbsp;
done and found that the functional benefits of&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:32.760 --> 02:42:39.840
sleep are not emergent when you are taking those&nbsp;
drugs, and that raised the red flag even more so.&nbsp;

02:42:39.840 --> 02:42:45.480
I don't think we have those studies yet for things&nbsp;
like trazodone, not at least in a very strict,&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:45.479 --> 02:42:51.479
specific way. So for me, I think I would&nbsp;
still want to warrant caution and look at&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:51.479 --> 02:42:55.080
those outcome measures long term.
Tim Ferriss: Agreed. Totally&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:42:55.080 --> 02:42:58.200
agreed. Yeah. Certainly for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

02:43:01.020 --> 02:43:11.281
learning fanatic, learning-obsessive person like&nbsp;
